---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import jurassicJumpImg from '../images/projects/jurassic-jump.jpg'
import supervimusImg from '../images/projects/supervimus.jpg'
import pasiLunchImg from '../images/projects/pasilunch.jpg'
import janneImg from '../images/projects/janne.jpg'
import sushiImg from '../images/projects/sushi.jpg'
import taMobileImg from '../images/projects/ta-mobile.jpg'
import Project from '../components/Project.astro'
---

<Layout
	title="Projects by André Vollrath"
	description="A collection of my frontend and game development projects."
	seo={{
		ogImage: pasiLunchImg,
		ogImageAlt: 'Projects page preview image',
		siteName: 'Andre Vollrath'
	}}
>
	<Project
		title="PasiLunch"
		htmlText={`
		<strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>PasiLunch</strong> is a small web service and Slack integration that aggregates daily lunch menus from restaurants near my office in Pasila, Helsinki.<br><br>

		Instead of checking multiple restaurant websites every day, PasiLunch collects the menus automatically and presents them in one place, either through a simple web interface or a Slack command.<br><br>

		The application is built with <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>Node.js</strong> and <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>Express</strong>, using <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>Cheerio</strong> to scrape menu data from restaurant websites. Results are cached and refreshed daily to keep the menus up to date while minimizing unnecessary requests.<br><br>

		The Slack integration adds a bit of personality with randomized humorous messages before displaying the menu results.<br><br>

		Check out today's lunch options: <a class='font-semibold underline text-magenta' href='https://lunchbot-btnu.onrender.com/'>PasiLunch website</a>
	`}
		projectImageSrc={pasiLunchImg}
		altProp="PasiLunch website"
		techStackLogos={[
			'HTML5.svg',
			'JavaScript.svg',
			'CSS 3.svg',
			'Node.js.svg',
			'Cheerio.svg',
			'Express.js.svg'
		]}
	/>

	<Project
		title="Jurassic Jump"
		buttonText="Click to load game"
		htmlText={`
			<strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>Jurassic Jump</strong> is a small jump-and-run game I built while exploring game development.<br><br>

			The project originally started as an experiment in <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>vanilla JavaScript</strong>, but as the game grew more complex I rebuilt it using the <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>Godot engine</strong> and <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>GDScript</strong>.<br><br>

			For the visuals I experimented with an AI-assisted workflow, creating reference images and transforming them into a Claymation-inspired style using <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>Affinity Photo</strong> and <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>ComfyUI</strong>.<br><br>

			Building Jurassic Jump introduced me to core game development concepts such as <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>level design</strong>, <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>sprite sheets</strong>, <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>particle systems</strong>, and <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>game state management</strong>.<br><br>

			You can also play it in full screen: <a class='font-semibold underline text-magenta' href='https://avollrath.github.io/WebGL-test/'>here</a>
		  `}
		projectImageSrc={jurassicJumpImg}
		altProp="Jurassic Jump Game"
		iframeSrc="https://avollrath.github.io/jurassic-jump/"
		techStackLogos={['Godot.svg']}
	/>

	<Project
		title="superVIMus"
		buttonText="Click to load game"
		htmlText={`
			<strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>superVIMus</strong> is a small puzzle game designed to build muscle memory for the <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>hjkl</strong> movement keys used in Vim.<br><br>

			The game combines simple box-pushing mechanics with playful pixel graphics and a slightly absurd twist, making it a fun way to practice keyboard navigation.<br><br>

			It was built with the <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>Godot engine</strong> using <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>GDScript</strong>, and explores concepts such as <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>grid-based movement</strong>, <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>level design</strong>, and <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>puzzle mechanics</strong>.<br><br>

			Try it out and sharpen your navigation skills: <a class='font-semibold underline text-magenta' href='https://avollrath.github.io/superVIMus/'>Play now</a>
		  `}
		projectImageSrc={supervimusImg}
		altProp="superVIMus Game"
		iframeSrc="https://avollrath.github.io/superVIMus/"
		techStackLogos={['Godot.svg']}
	/>

	<Project
		title="TalentAdore Mobile App"
		htmlText={`
		<strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>TalentAdore Mobile App</strong> is a mobile interface concept I designed for TalentAdore’s recruitment platform.<br><br>

		The goal was to translate a complex SaaS product into a clear and intuitive mobile experience. I designed the complete interface from scratch and created an interactive prototype in <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>Adobe XD</strong> to define navigation, user flows, and screen interactions.<br><br>

		The prototype served as the foundation for development. During implementation I worked closely with the engineering team to ensure the final product stayed aligned with the design vision and user experience goals.<br><br>

		This project highlights my approach to <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>UI design</strong>, <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>prototyping</strong>, and translating product requirements into intuitive mobile interfaces.
	`}
		projectImageSrc={taMobileImg}
		altProp="TalentAdore Mobile App UI"
		techStackLogos={['Adobe XD.svg']}
	/>

	<Project
		title="Janne Heikkinen Website"
		htmlText={`
		The <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>Janne Heikkinen Website</strong> was created for a Finnish member of parliament as part of a small team of three.<br><br>

		I was responsible for the visual design of the site, defining the layout, structure, and overall user experience. After the design prototype was completed, I also joined the development phase and contributed to the frontend implementation.<br><br>

		The project was built using an agile workflow and gave me the opportunity to combine <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>design ownership</strong> with hands-on <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>frontend development</strong> in a real client project.<br><br>

		Visit the live site: <a class='font-semibold underline text-magenta' href='https://janneheikkinen.fi/'>janneheikkinen.fi</a>
	`}
		projectImageSrc={janneImg}
		altProp="Janne Heikkinen Website"
		techStackLogos={['React.svg', 'SASS.svg', 'JavaScript.svg', 'GraphQL.svg', 'Gatsby.svg']}
	/>

	<Project
		title="Sushi-san Website"
		htmlText={`
		The <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>Sushi-san Website</strong> is a website I designed and developed for a sushi restaurant in Helsinki.<br><br>

		The goal was to create a clean and visually appealing online presence that reflects the restaurant’s brand while making it easy for visitors to explore the menu and essential information.<br><br>

		I handled both the <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>visual design</strong> and the <strong class='font-semibold text-dark-text'>frontend implementation</strong>, building the site from scratch based on the restaurant’s logo and color palette.<br><br>

		The result is a simple, responsive website that focuses on clarity, usability, and a strong visual presentation.<br><br>

	`}
		projectImageSrc={sushiImg}
		altProp="Sushi-san Website"
		techStackLogos={['HTML5.svg', 'CSS 3.svg']}
	/>
</Layout>
